// A builtin with a second name. character_code_at is charat under the name that
// says what it returns: the character code at an index, an int, not a one
// character string. Every later stage knows the builtin as charat, so a call by
// the new name is recorded under the old one, and means exactly what it means.
// Step one of the rename: the old name keeps working until the compiler's own
// uses have moved.

builtin_alias(string name) {
  string canon = name;
  if(name == "character_code_at") {
    canon = "charat";
  }
} return string canon;
("character_code_at"):("charat")
("charat"):("charat")
("len"):("len")
